@startuml 01-new-machine-setup
title Scenario 1: Set up a new machine (user-scope items)

actor User
participant "Terminal" as Term
participant "catalog.sh" as Cat
participant "GitHub\n(Eminakkoc/skills)" as Index
participant "Upstream sources\n(GitHub / npm)" as Up
participant "Claude Code CLI" as CC
database "<U+007E>/.claude" as Home
database "<U+007E>/.local/bin" as Bin

User -> Term : curl -fsSL .../catalog.sh | bash -s -- setup
Term -> Index : GET raw catalog.sh (main)
Index --> Term : catalog.sh
Term -> Cat : run "setup"

== Preflight ==
Cat -> Cat : check jq, gh, curl, claude on PATH
alt a prerequisite is missing
  Cat --> User : abort with install hint\n(e.g. "brew install jq")
end

== Resolve the index ==
Cat -> Index : resolve main -> commit SHA
Index --> Cat : index SHA
Cat -> Index : download tarball @ index SHA
Index --> Cat : catalog/, sources.json,\nskills/, hooks/, rules/
Cat -> Bin : install self as "catalog"

== Plan ==
Cat -> Cat : select items with scope = user, except tools\n(or only the items / bundles given)
Cat -> Cat : resolve "requires" (tools first)\nbin already on PATH -> recorded as "external"

== Install ==
loop each selected item
  alt kind = tool
    Cat -> Cat : bin already on PATH?
    opt missing
      Cat -> Up : npm install -g <package>@<pinned>
    end
  else kind = skill, source = self
    Cat -> Home : copy skills/<name>/ -> <U+007E>/.claude/skills/<name>/
  else kind = skill, third-party
    Cat -> Up : codeload <repo> tarball @ <pinned SHA>
    Up --> Cat : tarball
    Cat -> Home : extract <path> -> <U+007E>/.claude/skills/<name>/
  else kind = hook
    Cat -> Home : copy script -> <U+007E>/.claude/hooks/<name>/ (chmod +x)
    Cat -> Home : merge hook entry into <U+007E>/.claude/settings.json\n(command = <U+007E>/.claude/hooks/<name>/<script>)
  else kind = mcp
    Cat -> CC : claude mcp add --scope user <name> ...
  else kind = plugin
    Cat -> CC : claude plugin marketplace add <marketplaceRepo>\n(if not known yet)
    Cat -> CC : claude plugin install <plugin>@<marketplace>
    note right : version is decided by the\nmarketplace ("reviewed", not pinned)
  end
  Cat -> Home : record item in <U+007E>/.claude/catalog.lock.json\n(source, version, files written)
end

== Finish ==
Cat --> User : summary of installed items\n+ "restart Claude Code"
User -> CC : start claude
CC -> Home : loads user skills, hooks, MCPs, plugins
note over User, Home
  From here, the "catalog" skill is available in every session,
  so later requests can be made in plain words.
end note
@enduml
